import Mathlib

-- Declarations for this item will be appended below by the statement pipeline.

universe u

section

variable {F : Type u} [Group F] [IsFreeGroup F]

open Subgroup

-- Layer triage:
-- `source-facing`: elements `r₁ r₂ : F` of an arbitrary free group and a positive power relation
-- between their singleton normal closures.
-- `core/canonical`: `Subgroup.normalClosure` on singleton subsets of the ambient group.
-- `bridge/view`: the singleton normal closure is the source-facing relation, while the associated
-- one-relator quotient is only an auxiliary view; no separate quotient wrapper belongs in the
-- public statement.
-- Domain sampling:
-- 1. `Subgroup.normalClosure` is mathlib's owner construction for the normal subgroup generated by
--    a subset, so it is the correct owner abstraction for “is a consequence of `r₂`”.
-- 2. `Subgroup.normalClosure_subset_iff` is mathlib's canonical bridge from subset membership to
--    an inclusion of normal closures, so the singleton-inclusion reformulation is already
--    upstream and does not need a parallel local theorem here.
-- 3. `IsFreeGroup` is mathlib's owner abstraction for the intrinsic notion that the ambient group
--    is free, so the proposition stays on an abstract free group rather than choosing a basis.
-- 4. `conjugate_or_conjugate_inv_of_normalClosure_eq` from Proposition `2-5-7` is the chapter's
--    owner theorem for equality of singleton normal closures in an abstract free group, so the
--    current item should stay at the same owner level rather than introducing a quotient wrapper.
-- 5. `conjugate_or_conjugate_inv_of_mem_normalClosure_of_isPrimitiveElement` from Proposition
--    `2-5-14` is the adjacent chapter owner theorem for source-facing membership in a singleton
--    normal closure, confirming that normal-closure membership itself is already the right public
--    surface here.
-- Primitive vs. derived:
-- the primitive public data are only `r₁`, `r₂`, the positive integer `n`, and the hypothesis
-- that `r₁ ^ n` lies in the singleton normal closure generated by `r₂ ^ n`; passing to a
-- one-relator quotient is a derived proof view rather than primitive API data. The associated
-- singleton-normal-closure inclusion is likewise derived owner-level API, and its canonical
-- formulation already comes from `Subgroup.normalClosure_subset_iff`.

/-- Proposition 2-5-8: if `r₁` and `r₂` are elements of a free group and, for some positive
integer `n`, the power `r₁ ^ n` lies in the normal closure of `r₂ ^ n`, then `r₁` lies in the
normal closure of `r₂`. -/
-- Proof sketch: this is Magnus's root-extraction theorem for one-relator normal closures in a
-- free group. The hypothesis says that the `n`th power of `r₁` becomes trivial in the quotient by
-- the singleton normal closure generated by `r₂ ^ n`; Magnus's analysis of roots in free groups
-- then shows that the image of `r₁` is already trivial in the quotient by the singleton normal
-- closure generated by `r₂`, which is exactly the desired membership statement.
theorem mem_normalClosure_singleton_of_pow_mem_normalClosure_pow_singleton
    (r₁ r₂ : F) (n : ℕ+)
    (hpow : r₁ ^ (n : ℕ) ∈ normalClosure ({r₂ ^ (n : ℕ)})) :
    r₁ ∈ normalClosure ({r₂}) := sorry

end
